            <title>[LU-20947] o2iblnd: PUT_DONE on a finalised conn loses tx_conn with a send posted</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20947</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Problem"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;o2iblnd can call kiblnd_tx_complete() on a PUT_DONE tx with a NULL tx_conn. The node then crashes with a NULL pointer dereference. The crash needs a conn that finalises while the scheduler handles a PUT_ACK.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Environment"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Environment&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;master at 4a7bddaf15, and each branch that has a155c3fca38d ("&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-11756" title="kib_conn leak" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-11756"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-11756&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; o2iblnd: kib_conn leak").&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;o2ib with any HCA. The window is wider when a device removal or a reset closes conns under traffic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Reproduction"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Reproduction&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have no reproducer. We found the path in the source during a review of the &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-6132" title="Unable to unload ib drivers with lustre loaded" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-6132"&gt;LU-6132&lt;/a&gt; series.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Analysis"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Analysis&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;o2iblnd posts a PUT_REQ tx.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The PUT_ACK arrives before the PUT_REQ send completes. kiblnd_handle_rx() removes the tx from ibc_active_txs. tx_sending is still 1.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;connd finalises the conn and sets IBLND_CONN_DISCONNECTED. kiblnd_abort_txs() does not see the tx, because the tx is on no list.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kiblnd_handle_rx() calls kiblnd_queue_tx_locked() for the PUT_DONE. The DISCONNECTED branch puts the tx on ibc_zombie_txs, clears tx_conn, and drops the conn ref.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The HCA flushes the PUT_REQ send. kiblnd_tx_complete() reads tx-&amp;gt;tx_conn, which is NULL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;If the HCA does not flush, no code completes the posted send. kiblnd_destroy_conn() then hits LASSERT(conn-&amp;gt;ibc_nsends_posted == 0) when the last conn ref goes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Proposedfix"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Proposed fix&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the DISCONNECTED branch of kiblnd_queue_tx_locked(), keep a PUT_DONE with tx_sending != 0 on ibc_active_txs with its conn ref. The send completion then releases the tx through the normal idle path.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
